  "comment": "kiln.audio on the game client (enshrouded.exe 26430625 / svn 1287369). Evidence: docs/re/audio.md section 3, docs/kiln/services/audio.md. Keen's sound system (SoundSystem at app+0x21f80) plays a SoundContainerResource GUID in a scene: SoundStart(sys, 0, scene, &guid, &PlayParams{u64 0, i64 x/y/z 32.32 m, f32 volume, u8, u8 flags}) -> u32 instance id (index 20 bits, generation 12 bits; 0 = failed); SoundStop(sys, inst, fadeNs), SoundSetVolume(sys, inst, f32 0..1, fadeNs), SoundSetPosition(sys, inst, const i64[3]*), SoundIsPlaying(sys, inst) = the instance still exists (all four go through the instance lookup InstanceLookup(sys, inst)). SoundScenesInit(table, sys, reverb) runs once at start-up from the client state machine and fills table u32 scene[7] (keen::SoundSceneType Music, Ui, Game, Ambience, CharacterCreation, GlobalVoicechat, LoreVoiceover) and listener[7] at +0x1c. The voice-over manager (one per client game): VoiceoverRequest(mgr, &voGuid, speakerEntity, languageHint) sets the pending line (+vo.pending GUID, +vo.speaker, +vo.start); VoiceoverUpdate(mgr) (every frame, main thread) stops the old line and starts the new one in scene +vo.scene at +vo.position with volume +vo.volume, picking languages[slot of +vo.language]; VoiceoverSetPosition(mgr, const i64[3]*); VoiceoverLorePush(mgr, &voGuid, nameLoca, descriptionLoca, u16 version) is the lore (narration) queue push of the LoreVoiceover program (queue of 0x48-byte entries at +0x60, count byte +vo.lore_count, mode byte +vo.lore_mode: 0 play now, 1 queue, else drop; the head entry plays in scene +vo.lore_scene). SoundIsPlaying has no unique body (four 0x14-byte twins), so it is captured from its callers.",
